{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_27","type":"agent_message","text":"The function surface is already exact, but the two data exports revealed a real wrapper defect: the Rust `.so` exposed separate Rust statics while its embedded C implementation referenced renamed private copies. External writes to `g_debuglevel` therefore would not reach the implementation. I’m fixing the build so data symbols come directly from the embedded object, while functions remain trampoline-renamed."}}
